              "        color: #cccccc;\n",
              "    }\n",
              "    .sql-table tr:hover { background-color: #2a2d2e; }\n",
              "</style>\n",
              "<div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 1</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve employee_id and name for all employees.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> SELECT</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_id, employee_name FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_id</th><th>employee_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>102</td><td>Bob Johnson</td></tr><tr><td>103</td><td>Charlie Brown</td></tr><tr><td>104</td><td>David Lee</td></tr><tr><td>105</td><td>Eve Davis</td></tr><tr><td>106</td><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>107</td><td>Grace Taylor</td></tr><tr><td>108</td><td>Henry Wilson</td></tr><tr><td>109</td><td>Ivy Moore</td></tr><tr><td>110</td><td>Jack Green</td></tr><tr><td>111</td><td>Karen Hall</td></tr><tr><td>112</td><td>Liam King</td></tr><tr><td>113</td><td>Mia Wright</td></tr><tr><td>114</td><td>Noah Baker</td></tr><tr><td>115</td><td>Olivia Clark</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 2</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find all products with a price greater than 100.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> WHERE</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT product_name, price FROM products WHERE price > 100;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>product_name</th><th>price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laptop Pro</td><td>1200.0</td></tr><tr><td>Mechanical Keyboard</td><td>150.0</td></tr><tr><td>Desk Chair Ergonomic</td><td>300.0</td></tr><tr><td>LED Monitor 27 inch</td><td>250.0</td></tr><tr><td>External SSD 1TB</td><td>120.0</td></tr><tr><td>Router Wi-Fi 6</td><td>180.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 3</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Order customers by their signup date in ascending order.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> ORDER BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT customer_name, signup_date FROM customers ORDER BY signup_date ASC;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_name</th><th>signup_date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chris Purple</td><td>2021-08-15</td></tr><tr><td>Robert White</td><td>2021-09-01</td></tr><tr><td>Sarah Blue</td><td>2021-10-30</td></tr><tr><td>Jane Smith</td><td>2021-11-20</td></tr><tr><td>John Doe</td><td>2022-01-10</td></tr><tr><td>Michael Black</td><td>2022-01-25</td></tr><tr><td>Alice Brown</td><td>2022-02-15</td></tr><tr><td>Peter Jones</td><td>2022-03-05</td></tr><tr><td>Anna Yellow</td><td>2022-03-20</td></tr><tr><td>Emily Green</td><td>2022-04-12</td></tr><tr><td>David Grey</td><td>2022-05-01</td></tr><tr><td>Laura Red</td><td>2022-06-01</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 4</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve all unique cities where customers are located.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> DISTINCT</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT DISTINCT city FROM customers;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>city</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New York</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td></tr><tr><td>Chicago</td></tr><tr><td>Houston</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 5</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Get the top 3 highest paid employees.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> LIMIT</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary FROM employees ORDER BY salary DESC LIMIT 3;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 6</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Count the total number of employees.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> Aggregates</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_employees FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>total_employees</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>15</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 7</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Calculate the total revenue (sum of total_amount) from all orders.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> Aggregates</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT SUM(total_amount) AS total_revenue FROM orders;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>total_revenue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4344.99</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 8</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find the average salary of all employees.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> Aggregates</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT AVG(salary) AS avg_salary FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>avg_salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>71133.33333333333</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 9</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve the minimum and maximum product prices.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> Aggregates</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT MIN(price) AS min_price, MAX(price) AS max_price FROM products;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>min_price</th><th>max_price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10.0</td><td>1200.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 10</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find employees in department 3 with a salary greater than 80,000.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> WHERE</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary FROM employees WHERE department_id = 3 AND salary > 80000;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 11</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List all products that belong to either 'Electronics' or 'Appliances'.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> IN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT product_name, category FROM products WHERE category IN ('Electronics', 'Appliances');</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>product_name</th><th>category</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laptop Pro</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>Gaming Mouse</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>Mechanical Keyboard</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>LED Monitor 27 inch</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>Coffee Maker</td><td>Appliances</td></tr><tr><td>Blender High Power</td><td>Appliances</td></tr><tr><td>Smart Speaker</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>External SSD 1TB</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>Webcam HD</td><td>Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>Router Wi-Fi 6</td><td>Electronics</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 12</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find employees hired between '2020-01-01' and '2021-12-31'.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> BETWEEN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, hire_date FROM employees WHERE hire_date BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2021-12-31';</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>hire_date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>2020-01-15</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>2020-03-01</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>2021-06-20</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>2020-11-01</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>2020-09-01</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>2021-01-01</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>2020-12-12</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>2021-02-14</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 13</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List all employees and their corresponding department names using a JOIN.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> JOIN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT e.employee_name, d.department_name FROM employees e JOIN departments d ON e.department_id = d.department_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>department_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>Sales</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>Sales</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>Sales</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>Marketing</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>Marketing</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>Engineering</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>Engineering</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>Engineering</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>HR</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>HR</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>Finance</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>Finance</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>Engineering</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>Sales</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>Engineering</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 14</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find the names of all employees who work in the 'Sales' department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> JOIN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT e.employee_name FROM employees e JOIN departments d ON e.department_id = d.department_id WHERE d.department_name = 'Sales';</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 15</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List all departments and any associated employees, including departments without employees.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> LEFT JOIN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT d.department_name, e.employee_name FROM departments d LEFT JOIN employees e ON d.department_id = e.department_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>department_name</th><th>employee_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Bob Johnson</td></tr><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Charlie Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Noah Baker</td></tr><tr><td>Marketing</td><td>David Lee</td></tr><tr><td>Marketing</td><td>Eve Davis</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering</td><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering</td><td>Grace Taylor</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering</td><td>Henry Wilson</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering</td><td>Mia Wright</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering</td><td>Olivia Clark</td></tr><tr><td>HR</td><td>Ivy Moore</td></tr><tr><td>HR</td><td>Jack Green</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Karen Hall</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Liam King</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 16</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Count the number of employees in each department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> GROUP BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT department_id, COUNT(*) AS emp_count FROM employees GROUP BY department_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>department_id</th><th>emp_count</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 17</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Calculate the total salary expenditure for each department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> GROUP BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT department_id, SUM(salary) AS total_salary FROM employees GROUP BY department_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>department_id</th><th>total_salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>257000</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>125000</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>424000</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>115000</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>146000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 18</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find the average product price for each product category.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> GROUP BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT category, AVG(price) AS avg_price FROM products GROUP BY category;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>category</th><th>avg_price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Appliances</td><td>90.0</td></tr><tr><td>Electronics</td><td>266.87375</td></tr><tr><td>Furniture</td><td>300.0</td></tr><tr><td>Stationery</td><td>17.5</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 19</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Sort all employees by department_id (ASC) and then by salary (DESC).</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> ORDER BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, department_id, salary FROM employees ORDER BY department_id ASC, salary DESC;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>department_id</th><th>salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>1</td><td>75000</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>1</td><td>62000</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>2</td><td>70000</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>2</td><td>55000</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>3</td><td>92000</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>3</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>3</td><td>82000</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>4</td><td>65000</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>4</td><td>50000</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>5</td><td>78000</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>5</td><td>68000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 20</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find all products whose names start with the letter 'L'.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Beginner | <b>Topic:</b> LIKE</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT product_name FROM products WHERE product_name LIKE 'L%';</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>product_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laptop Pro</td></tr><tr><td>LED Monitor 27 inch</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 21</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List department IDs that have more than 2 employees.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> HAVING</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT department_id FROM employees GROUP BY department_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 2;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>department_id</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 22</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Show the order ID, product name, and quantity for every order item.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> JOIN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT oi.order_id, p.product_name, oi.quantity FROM order_items oi JOIN products p ON oi.product_id = p.product_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>order_id</th><th>product_name</th><th>quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1001</td><td>Laptop Pro</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1001</td><td>Gaming Mouse</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1002</td><td>Desk Chair Ergonomic</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1003</td><td>Mechanical Keyboard</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1004</td><td>LED Monitor 27 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1005</td><td>Coffee Maker</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1006</td><td>Blender High Power</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1007</td><td>External SSD 1TB</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1008</td><td>Notebook A5</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1009</td><td>Smart Speaker</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1010</td><td>Webcam HD</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1011</td><td>Router Wi-Fi 6</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1012</td><td>Pen Set Premium</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1013</td><td>External SSD 1TB</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1014</td><td>Desk Chair Ergonomic</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1015</td><td>Gaming Mouse</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1016</td><td>Laptop Pro</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1001</td><td>Gaming Mouse</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 23</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find employees who are paid more than the overall average salary.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Subquery</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary FROM employees WHERE salary > (SELECT AVG(salary) FROM employees);</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>80000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 24</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Show each employee name, their salary, and the average salary of their specific department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Scalar Subquery</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT e1.employee_name, e1.salary, (SELECT AVG(e2.salary) FROM employees e2 WHERE e2.department_id = e1.department_id) as dept_avg FROM employees e1;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th><th>dept_avg</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td><td>64250.0</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>60000</td><td>64250.0</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>62000</td><td>64250.0</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>70000</td><td>62500.0</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>55000</td><td>62500.0</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td><td>84800.0</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>80000</td><td>84800.0</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td><td>84800.0</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>65000</td><td>57500.0</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>50000</td><td>57500.0</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td><td>73000.0</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>68000</td><td>73000.0</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td><td>84800.0</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>60000</td><td>64250.0</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>80000</td><td>84800.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 25</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Categorize employees as 'High' if salary > 70000, else 'Low'.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> CASE</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary, CASE WHEN salary > 70000 THEN 'High' ELSE 'Low' END as salary_level FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th><th>salary_level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>60000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>62000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>70000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>55000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>80000</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>65000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>50000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>68000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>60000</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>80000</td><td>High</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 26</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve the character length of every product name.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT product_name, LENGTH(product_name) AS name_len FROM products;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>product_name</th><th>name_len</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laptop Pro</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Gaming Mouse</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Mechanical Keyboard</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>Desk Chair Ergonomic</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>LED Monitor 27 inch</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>Coffee Maker</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Blender High Power</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>Smart Speaker</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>External SSD 1TB</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>Notebook A5</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><td>Pen Set Premium</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Webcam HD</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>Router Wi-Fi 6</td><td>14</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 27</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Count the total number of orders placed in each year.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Date Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT strftime('%Y', order_date) AS order_year, COUNT(*) AS order_count FROM orders GROUP BY 1;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>order_year</th><th>order_count</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2022</td><td>16</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 28</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Calculate the days between the earliest and latest customer signup.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Date Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT julianday(MAX(signup_date)) - julianday(MIN(signup_date)) AS days_diff FROM customers;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>days_diff</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>290.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 29</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve a unique list of all names present in both Employees and Customers tables.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> UNION</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name FROM employees UNION SELECT customer_name FROM customers;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Anna Yellow</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Chris Purple</td></tr><tr><td>David Grey</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td></tr><tr><td>Emily Green</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td></tr><tr><td>Jane Smith</td></tr><tr><td>John Doe</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td></tr><tr><td>Laura Red</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td></tr><tr><td>Michael Black</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td></tr><tr><td>Peter Jones</td></tr><tr><td>Robert White</td></tr><tr><td>Sarah Blue</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 30</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Combine all employee and customer names into one list, including duplicates.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> UNION ALL</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name FROM employees UNION ALL SELECT customer_name FROM customers;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td></tr><tr><td>John Doe</td></tr><tr><td>Jane Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Peter Jones</td></tr><tr><td>Alice Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Robert White</td></tr><tr><td>Emily Green</td></tr><tr><td>Michael Black</td></tr><tr><td>Sarah Blue</td></tr><tr><td>David Grey</td></tr><tr><td>Laura Red</td></tr><tr><td>Chris Purple</td></tr><tr><td>Anna Yellow</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 31</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find all customers who have placed at least one order.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> EXISTS</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT customer_name FROM customers c WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM orders o WHERE o.customer_id = c.customer_id);</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>John Doe</td></tr><tr><td>Jane Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Peter Jones</td></tr><tr><td>Alice Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Robert White</td></tr><tr><td>Emily Green</td></tr><tr><td>Michael Black</td></tr><tr><td>Sarah Blue</td></tr><tr><td>David Grey</td></tr><tr><td>Laura Red</td></tr><tr><td>Chris Purple</td></tr><tr><td>Anna Yellow</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 32</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Identify customers who have never placed an order.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> NOT EXISTS</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT customer_name FROM customers c WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM orders o WHERE o.customer_id = c.customer_id);</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><p style='color:#aaa;'><i>No results found for this query.</i></p></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 33</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List all employees along with their manager's name.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Self Join</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT e.employee_name, m.employee_name as manager_name FROM employees e LEFT JOIN employees m ON e.manager_id = m.employee_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>manager_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>David Lee</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>Ivy Moore</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>Karen Hall</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>Frank White</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>Alice Smith</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>Frank White</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 34</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find product categories that contain more than 3 distinct products.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> HAVING</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT category FROM products GROUP BY category HAVING COUNT(*) > 3;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>category</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Electronics</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 35</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve the second highest unique salary from the company.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> OFFSET</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT DISTINCT salary FROM employees ORDER BY salary DESC LIMIT 1 OFFSET 1;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>90000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 36</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Calculate the total quantity of units sold for each product_id.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> GROUP BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT product_id, SUM(quantity) AS total_units FROM order_items GROUP BY product_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>product_id</th><th>total_units</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 37</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find customer IDs for individuals who have placed more than one order.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> HAVING</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) FROM orders GROUP BY customer_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>COUNT(*)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 38</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List products that have never been included in an order item.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> LEFT JOIN</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT p.product_name FROM products p LEFT JOIN order_items oi ON p.product_id = oi.product_id WHERE oi.order_id IS NULL;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><p style='color:#aaa;'><i>No results found for this query.</i></p></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 39</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find the single highest salary within each department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> GROUP BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT department_id, MAX(salary) AS max_salary FROM employees GROUP BY department_id;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>department_id</th><th>max_salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>75000</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>70000</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>92000</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>65000</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>78000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 40</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find the names of customers who placed an order in the month of March.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Intermediate | <b>Topic:</b> Dates</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT DISTINCT c.customer_name FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id WHERE strftime('%m', o.order_date) = '03';</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Brown</td></tr><tr><td>Robert White</td></tr><tr><td>Jane Smith</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 41</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find employees paid above their department average using a CTE.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> CTE</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>WITH DeptAvg AS (SELECT department_id, AVG(salary) as av FROM employees GROUP BY 1) SELECT e.employee_name, e.salary FROM employees e JOIN DeptAvg d ON e.department_id = d.department_id WHERE e.salary > d.av;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, grouping data for aggregation, filtering with conditions, utilizing common table expressions (CTEs), to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>70000</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>65000</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 42</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find the employee(s) with the 2nd highest salary in each department using RANK.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Window Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary, department_id FROM (SELECT employee_name, salary, department_id, RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY department_id ORDER BY salary DESC) as r FROM employees) WHERE r = 2;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, using window functions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th><th>department_id</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>62000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>55000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>50000</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>68000</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 43</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Retrieve the top 2 earners per department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Window Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary, department_id FROM (SELECT employee_name, salary, department_id, RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY department_id ORDER BY salary DESC) as r FROM employees) WHERE r <= 2;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including filtering with conditions, using window functions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th><th>department_id</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>62000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>70000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>55000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>65000</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>50000</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>68000</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 44</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Calculate the Dense Rank of salaries within each department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Window Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, department_id, salary, DENSE_RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY department_id ORDER BY salary DESC) AS d_rank FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including using window functions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>department_id</th><th>salary</th><th>d_rank</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>1</td><td>75000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>1</td><td>62000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>2</td><td>70000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>2</td><td>55000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>3</td><td>92000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>3</td><td>90000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>3</td><td>82000</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>4</td><td>65000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>4</td><td>50000</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>5</td><td>78000</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>5</td><td>68000</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 45</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> For each employee, show the salary of the next highest-paid person in their department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Window Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary, department_id, LEAD(salary) OVER(PARTITION BY department_id ORDER BY salary) AS next_salary FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including using window functions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th><th>department_id</th><th>next_salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>60000</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>60000</td><td>1</td><td>62000</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>62000</td><td>1</td><td>75000</td></tr><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td><td>1</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>55000</td><td>2</td><td>70000</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>70000</td><td>2</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>80000</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>80000</td><td>3</td><td>82000</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td><td>3</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td><td>3</td><td>92000</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td><td>3</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>50000</td><td>4</td><td>65000</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>65000</td><td>4</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>68000</td><td>5</td><td>78000</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td><td>5</td><td>NULL</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 46</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> For each employee, show the salary of the person paid immediately less than them in their department.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Window Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT employee_name, salary, department_id, LAG(salary) OVER(PARTITION BY department_id ORDER BY salary) AS prev_salary FROM employees;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including using window functions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>employee_name</th><th>salary</th><th>department_id</th><th>prev_salary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bob Johnson</td><td>60000</td><td>1</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Noah Baker</td><td>60000</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td></tr><tr><td>Charlie Brown</td><td>62000</td><td>1</td><td>60000</td></tr><tr><td>Alice Smith</td><td>75000</td><td>1</td><td>62000</td></tr><tr><td>Eve Davis</td><td>55000</td><td>2</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>David Lee</td><td>70000</td><td>2</td><td>55000</td></tr><tr><td>Grace Taylor</td><td>80000</td><td>3</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Olivia Clark</td><td>80000</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>Henry Wilson</td><td>82000</td><td>3</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>Frank White</td><td>90000</td><td>3</td><td>82000</td></tr><tr><td>Mia Wright</td><td>92000</td><td>3</td><td>90000</td></tr><tr><td>Jack Green</td><td>50000</td><td>4</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Ivy Moore</td><td>65000</td><td>4</td><td>50000</td></tr><tr><td>Liam King</td><td>68000</td><td>5</td><td>NULL</td></tr><tr><td>Karen Hall</td><td>78000</td><td>5</td><td>68000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 47</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Calculate the running total of order amounts for every customer.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Window Functions</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT customer_id, order_date, total_amount, SUM(total_amount) OVER(PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY order_date) AS running_total FROM orders;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including using window functions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>order_date</th><th>total_amount</th><th>running_total</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>2022-01-15</td><td>1275.0</td><td>1275.0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2022-02-01</td><td>150.0</td><td>1425.0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2022-04-10</td><td>99.99</td><td>1524.99</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2022-05-10</td><td>120.0</td><td>1644.99</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2022-01-20</td><td>300.0</td><td>300.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2022-03-25</td><td>120.0</td><td>420.0</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2022-02-10</td><td>250.0</td><td>250.0</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2022-03-01</td><td>100.0</td><td>100.0</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2022-03-15</td><td>80.0</td><td>80.0</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2022-04-01</td><td>10.0</td><td>10.0</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2022-04-15</td><td>60.0</td><td>60.0</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>2022-05-01</td><td>180.0</td><td>180.0</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>2022-05-05</td><td>25.0</td><td>25.0</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>2022-05-15</td><td>300.0</td><td>300.0</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>2022-06-01</td><td>75.0</td><td>75.0</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>2022-06-05</td><td>1200.0</td><td>1200.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 48</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Rank customers by their total lifetime spending.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> GROUP BY</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT customer_id, SUM(total_amount) AS ltv FROM orders GROUP BY customer_id ORDER BY ltv DESC;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including grouping data for aggregation, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>ltv</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>1644.99</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>1200.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>420.0</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>300.0</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>250.0</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>180.0</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>100.0</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>80.0</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>75.0</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>60.0</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>25.0</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>10.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 49</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> List products ordered by customers residing in 'New York'.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> Subquery</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>SELECT DISTINCT p.product_name FROM products p JOIN order_items oi ON p.product_id = oi.product_id WHERE oi.order_id IN (SELECT order_id FROM orders WHERE customer_id IN (SELECT customer_id FROM customers WHERE city = 'New York'));</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, filtering with conditions, to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>product_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laptop Pro</td></tr><tr><td>Gaming Mouse</td></tr><tr><td>Mechanical Keyboard</td></tr><tr><td>Coffee Maker</td></tr><tr><td>Smart Speaker</td></tr><tr><td>Router Wi-Fi 6</td></tr><tr><td>External SSD 1TB</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='sql-container'><h3>QUESTION 50</h3><p><b>Problem:</b> Find customers who have purchased both 'Laptop Pro' AND 'Gaming Mouse'.</p><p><b>Difficulty:</b> Advanced | <b>Topic:</b> CTE</p><b>SQL SOLUTION:</b><pre><code>WITH L AS (SELECT o.customer_id FROM orders o JOIN order_items oi ON o.order_id = oi.order_id JOIN products p ON oi.product_id = p.product_id WHERE p.product_name = 'Laptop Pro'), M AS (SELECT o.customer_id FROM orders o JOIN order_items oi ON o.order_id = oi.order_id JOIN products p ON oi.product_id = p.product_id WHERE p.product_name = 'Gaming Mouse') SELECT customer_name FROM customers WHERE customer_id IN L AND customer_id IN M;</code></pre><p><b>Explanation:</b> This query selects data based on logic including joining multiple tables, filtering with conditions, utilizing common table expressions (CTEs), to solve the specific requirement.</p><b>Sample Input/Output:</b><div class='sql-table-wrapper'><table class='sql-table'><thead><tr><th>customer_name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>John Doe</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>"
